        "kind": "ai-tool-descriptor",
        "id": "tool:your-files",
        "label": "Your files",
        "job": "Every name of the person's files, listed, followed as it changes, read by range, written, moved, shared and released, for an AI or a device's folder, through the engine's one door",
        "description": "The person's files (tools/live-namespace) as a session the engine keeps open and reaches only by calls: tools:run at @tools {tool: \"tool:your-files\", call: {name, arguments}} sends one MCP tools/call to the account's one session of this row, which the first call starts (trillion-rust src/tool_runs/tools/sessions.rs `call`); each call is answered on its own, so a list_changes that waits holds back no read. `name` is an operation of mcp-tools.json: list_files, list_changes, show_item, read_file_span, write_file, write_file_start, write_file_piece, write_file_finish, move_names, set_aside, put_back, make_folder, set_pin_rule, thumbnail, bounds, this_computer and the rest. The answer is {tool, result} with the operation's answer in result.structuredContent; a refusal is result.isError with {code, outcome}. read_file_span with raw: true answers the span's bytes themselves: {byte_slice: {total, offset, length, base64}}, or, to a request that accepts application/octet-stream, the raw bytes as the HTTP body with X-Total-Bytes and X-Offset (session.byte_result), so they cross the wire once, the first of them as soon as the store sends it. write_file_piece takes its piece raw the same way: a POST whose Content-Type is application/octet-stream, whose body is the piece and whose X-Call header is the base64url of the tools/call JSON; the engine names the body it kept as the call's content_file (session.byte_argument). The run opens no port. Its names are rows in the person's own Postgres database (own-rows-postgres-connection, reached on the loopback port the computer reports as own-rows-postgres); its bytes are the person's own files-store connection, each field mounted on the descriptor settings.json `attached` names and never printed. The program is the live-namespace this computer keeps among its program folders.",
        "status": "active",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {}
        },
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "A call answers {tool, result: {structuredContent, content, isError}} or {tool, error}; the session's start answers its state."
        },
        "invoke": {
          "kind": "container",
          "programs": {
            "live-namespace": {
              "search": "live-namespace"
            }
          },
          "argv": [
            "live-namespace",
            "mcp",
            "--state",
            {
              "fill": {
                "from": "task",
                "field": "kept_folder"
              }
            },
            "--computer",
            {
              "fill": {
                "from": "computer"
              }
            }
          ],
          "session": {
            "keep_open": true,
            "calls": true,
            "byte_result": "bytes",
            "byte_argument": "content_file"
          },
          "kept_folder": true,
          "internet": true,
          "local_doors": [
            "own-rows-postgres"
          ],
          "credential_mounts": [
            {
              "secret_name": "files-store-secret",
              "fd": 3
            },
            {
              "secret_name": "files-store-key-id",
              "fd": 4
            },
            {
              "secret_name": "files-store-bucket",
              "fd": 5
            },
            {
              "secret_name": "files-store-endpoint",
              "fd": 6
            },
            {
              "secret_name": "files-store-region",
              "fd": 7
            },
            {
              "secret_name": "own-rows-postgres-connection",
              "fd": 8
            }
          ]
        },
        "maker": "maker:live-namespace",
        "licence_class": "licence:maker-own",
        "placements": [
          "placement:your-computer"
        ],
        "provenance": {
          "source": "Trillion-X/trillion-rust src/account_files at 5fbc2ff4b1 (moved into tools/live-namespace), over its own rows in SQL (src/store)"
        }
      }
    }
